course: dictionary
lesson: 6163
title: Finding the meaning of miner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A miner is a person who digs under the ground to get coal, gold, metal or stones. When you meet a word you don't know, read the words around it, because they are its context. «Metal rivets on jeans were patented to stop pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.» Work trousers and tearing pockets tell you that miners do hard work.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Canaries were carried underground by coal miners.» If you read "a person who digs under the ground for coal" instead of miners, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues about where the word happens. «Humphry Davy made a safety lamp for coal miners in 1815.» The lamp was made for mines, so a miner works in a mine. Context gives you a clear picture, and a dictionary can check it when you are unsure.
fact: A miner is a person who digs under the ground to get coal, gold, metal or stones.
fact: «Coal miners once worked 6 days of 10 hours, which is 60 hours a week.»
fact: Long ago, coal miners carried canaries underground, because a canary showed the effects of bad gas before people noticed it.
fact: Humphry Davy's safety lamp of 1815 had a metal mesh around the flame, which stopped it lighting explosive gas in the mine.
fact: A «gold miner» is a miner who digs for gold.
exercise: «Humphry Davy made a safety lamp for coal miners in 1815.» What is a miner? | A kind of small bird | A tool for lighting fires | A person who sells bread | *A person who digs under the ground for coal, gold, metal or stones
exercise: «Coal miners once worked 6 days of 10 hours, which is 60 hours a week.» How many hours a week did coal miners once work? | 6 | 40 | 10 | *60
exercise: «Long ago coal miners carried canaries underground because a canary showed the effects of bad gas.» Why did they carry canaries? | *To warn them about bad gas before people noticed it | To keep the mine warm | Because canaries are very large birds | To find gold for the miners
test: «Tunnel-boring machines are often given women's names, from an old tradition linked to Saint Barbara, the saint of miners.» Saint Barbara is linked to which group of people? | Pirates | Sailors | *Miners | Farmers
test: What does a «gold miner» do? | *Digs under the ground to get gold | Cooks gold cakes | Paints gold pictures | Sells gold in a shop
exam: Jade reads «Metal rivets on jeans were patented in 1873 to stop pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.» What is the best way to work out what miners means? | *Read the words around it, then try your meaning in the sentence | Skip the whole text and never come back to it | Guess it is a type of trousers | Say the word out loud and stop reading
